# Normalize line endings so a checkout is byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Without this file, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true rewrites text
# files to CRLF on checkout. Test expectations written as C# raw string literals
# then carry CRLF, while the product printers emit "\n", so those tests fail on
# Windows and pass on Linux CI. See #3526.
#
# eol=lf pins the working-tree ending rather than only the stored one, so the
# literals stay LF on Windows too.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed by tooling that treats a trailing CR as part of the
# interpreter path or argument, so they must stay LF regardless of the above.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary payloads must never be line-ending converted. fixture.nettrace is the
# only such file committed today; the rest are listed because this repository
# reads assemblies and package artifacts, and a future fixture that Git guessed
# wrong about would be corrupted silently.
*.nettrace binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.nupkg binary
*.snupkg binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
